lensd.spec.md E0 W1 H0 │  1   # lensd specification
 §0 Definitions        │  2
  §0.1 Time            │  3   What lensd guarantees, as definitions (`**Def $Name (title).**`) and
   ◦ $Time.Media       │      invariants
   ◦ $Time.Wall        │  4   (`**$Name (title).**`). Normative statements use
   ◦ $Time.Elapsed     │  5   MUST. Every invariant names what checks it: a TLA+ model in spec/tla/
  §0.2 Intervals and ne│      (each with a deliberately broken
   ◦ $Interval         │  6   "mutant" that TLC must reject), a Go test, or a runtime check. Go
   ◦ $Interval.Gap     │      tests cite what they check with a
 §1 Frames, segments an│  7   comment directly above the test:
  • $Frame.Timing      │  8
  • $Frame.SegmentShape│  9       // Spec: $Frame.Timing §1 "quoted text from this file"
  • $Frame.Numbering   │ 10
  • $Frame.OneWriter   │ 11   and code may cite the invariant it enforces (`// $Sdk.NvrAgrees:
  • $Frame.CleanGenerat│      ...`). A spec change and the matching test
  • $Frame.Forward     │ 12   or model change go in the same commit. Values marked (code: …) also
  • $Frame.InitFixed   │      exist as constants; changing one
 §2 HLS hub (transcoder│ 13   means changing the other. Liveness is stated as bounded-time rules on
  • $Hub.TranscoderCap │      lensd's own clock ($Time.Elapsed),
  • $Hub.TakenOver     │ 14   not as TLA+ liveness properties. Trace verification (checking runtime
  • $Hub.IdleStop      │      traces against the models) is out
  • $Hub.BlockingAnswer│ 15   of scope.
  • $Hub.MemoryBound   │ 16
 §3 Live relay         │ 17   ## Context (for readers without the code)
  • $Relay.OneSession  │ 18
  • $Relay.NoOrphans   │ 19   lensd is a Go web gateway for two NVRs at one site. It relays live
